      ],
      "source": "https://www.watsekacity.org/community/page/about-us",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Old Iroquois County Courthouse, built in 1866 and expanded in 1881 and 1927, is the only U.S. courthouse constructed entirely with private funds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watseka%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Watseka sits on the historic Hubbard Trail, a key route that helped the community grow as settlers moved into Illinois prairie.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitwatseka.com/history.html",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the 1967 Centennial Celebration, the Iroquois County Historical Society was formed to preserve the town’s heritage and protect the courthouse.",
